From 0b1b5ceab0af9acea2ad4a5b93161c5cd865a260 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:50:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] estserver: no mock CA; the TACRA backend alone, and a strict
 configuration

The server created a mock CA at every start (a transient one when the
configuration named none), issued its own TLS certificate from it when
the configuration had no tls section, and used it as the CA behind the
EST resources unless a tacra or attest section replaced it. The server
now runs only with the TACRA backend: the mock CA, the mock attested CA
(attest) and the self-issued server certificate are removed, and the tls
and tacra sections are required. With tacra always present, TLS 1.3 is
always the minimum.

The configuration is decoded strictly: mock_ca, attest, any field the
server does not know, or data after the object is an error, where it
was ignored before. The sample and estserver.json.example are in the
TACRA backend's shape. config_test.go checks that both parse, and that
the mock CA's sections, a missing section, a missing key file and a
misspelt field are refused.

internal/mockca stays for the upstream tests that use it; the server no
longer imports it.
